{
  "statement": "A reminder is what they asked to be told about. \"Remind me\" and \"don't let me forget\" set the flag on a task or an event; a fact with a date does not, and a standing fact is a note with no flag.",
  "why": "A date is not announced; a reminder is. The two digests read the flag and nothing else, so a date filed as a reminder pushes a fact somebody never asked to hear again, and a request filed without it is a reminder that never arrives. The flag is the difference between the calendar and the nagging, and the person chose which by how they said it.",
  "sources": [
    "024 AC-4, AC-23",
    "006: is_reminder on a task or an event",
    "plan_v2.md: A reminder is not a type"
  ],
